    {
      "content": "Pulls a list of new CrowdStrike Detections, flags them as in progress in CrowdStrike, and gets the detection details for each one.\n\nFor each detection, the individual behaviors are examined, and the process hash is checked in VirusTotal to see if it is known malicious.\n\nWhere there is a provided IOC as part of the behavior, this is also checked in VirusTotal.\n\nA Jira ticket is created for each Detection, and a message sent to a Slack channel. \n",
      "position": [
        1650,
        -1020
      ],
      "guid": "c0d8cab4ba664406884c9b7d02f0123d",
      "width": 270
    },
    {
      "content": "# **Requirements**\n\n## **Credentials**\n - [ ] `crowdstrike` - Your [CrowdStrike API Token](https://explained.tines.com/en/articles/7950192-crowdstrike-authentication-guide) with the scopes:\n    - `Detection:Read`\n    - `Detection:Write`\n    - `Hosts:Read`\n    - `Hosts:Write`\n    - `Real Time Response:Read`\n    - `Real Time Response:Write`\n - [ ] `jira` - Your API key for [Jira](https://explained.tines.com/en/articles/7969792-atlassian-authentication-guide)\n - [ ] `virustotal` - The API key for your [VirusTotal](https://explained.tines.com/en/articles/7853769-virustotal-authentication-guide) \n\n## **Resources**\n - [ ] `crowdstrike_domain` - Your CrowdStrike instance domain\n- [ ] `jira_domain` - Your Jira instance domain\n- [ ] `jira_username`- The Jira username associated with your API token\n- [ ] `slack_url` - A Slack channel webhook URL",
      "position": [
        1350,
        -1020
      ],
      "guid": "0697ed9289f5632e39efd7f7bf90a089",
      "width": 270
    }
  ],
